// Elementum — the town's real problems (Barbara, 2026-11-22: "make actual problems … 50 different scenarios with books").
// Every problem belongs to someone in town. Walk up, be curious and ask; frame it; read (lessons + library books); pick an idea;
// build it yourself in the right workshop (eng_struct / eng_garden / eng_water / eng_heat); test it. Each has 3 levels.
// Fields: id, eng, owner, title, says (what they grumble about), facts(L) → [question, answer], need/test (for framing),
// cons(L) → the real constraints, lessons, books (library questions), ideas, levels [L1, L2, L3].
